{
  "found": true,
  "answer": "Everglades is the largest subtropical wilderness in the US and home to alligators, American crocodiles, manatees, and wading birds. You can see alligators and wading birds concentrated around waterholes during the dry season, or walk along boardwalks like the Kirby Storter Boardwalk in Big Cypress to experience the cypress swamps and sawgrass prairies.",
  "sources": [1, 2]
}

{
  "found": true,
  "answer": "You can view the glowing lava crater at night from the scenic overlooks along the edge of the Kīlauea caldera, such as Kīlauea Overlook and Uēkahuna, where intermittent eruptions in the Halemaʻumaʻu crater provide a stunning view after dark.",
  "sources": [1, 2, 3]
}

{
  "found": true,
  "answer": "Sprague Lake in Rocky Mountain National Park features an easy, wheelchair-accessible 1.3-kilometer loop trail with stunning views of the Continental Divide, and you can take the Hiker Shuttle from the Estes Park Visitor Center to get there.",
  "sources": [2, 4]
}

